---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ProjectPageHeader from '../ProjectPageHeader.astro';
import ProjectSection from '../ProjectSection.astro';
import ProjectList from '../ProjectList.astro';
import ProjectProse from '../ProjectProse.astro';
import TagList from '../TagList.astro';
---

<Base title="Simmer / Kacper Noniewicz" description="Replacement software for the Monsieur Cuisine Connect kitchen robot, with tested motor safety, a phone companion and an API for agents.">
  <div class="py-16 pb-20">
    <ProjectPageHeader label="Kotlin / Android / MIT / Release planned" title="Simmer" intro="Replacement software for the Lidl Monsieur Cuisine Connect (SKMC 1100 A1) kitchen robot. A fast cooking app on the robot's own tablet, a companion web app the robot serves to your phone, and an API that lets agents plan meals without ever starting the motor." />

    <div class="max-w-180">
      <ProjectSection title="What it does">
        <ProjectList items={[
          "Guided cooking, manual mode, programs and the scale, on the robot's Android 6 tablet",
          "Motor safety in a pure-Kotlin core with unit tests: no spinning with the lid open, ramped speeds for hot contents, faults that latch until acknowledged",
          "A companion web app (Preact) for the meal plan, recipes, shopping list and prep, served by the robot itself",
          "A REST API (38 operations) and an MCP server (17 tools), both under golden tests; anything an agent sends lands in review first",
          "A Home Assistant integration: live cooking state, alerts, and the shopping list as a two-way to-do list",
        ]} />
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Why">
        <ProjectProse>
          <p>The hardware is good and the stock app is slow. Rooting the tablet turned a closed appliance into a device I could shape around how I actually cook: pick a recipe, add it to the plan, and the shopping list is already in Home Assistant.</p>
          <p>The full story is in the <a href="/blog/simmer/">Simmer write-up</a>.</p>
        </ProjectProse>
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Stack">
        <TagList tags={["Kotlin", "Android", "Preact", "MCP", "Home Assistant"]} />
      </ProjectSection>

      <ProjectSection title="Status">
        <ProjectProse>
          <p>Cooking with it daily. A fork of <a href="https://github.com/Wuki60/MrCuisineVibeConnect" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">MrCuisineVibeConnect</a> (MIT). Independent project, not affiliated with Lidl, SilverCrest or Hoyer.</p>
        </ProjectProse>
      </ProjectSection>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
